---
description: Quality gates and required test focus.
globs: '{src/**,test/**,tests/**,playwright/**}'
alwaysApply: false
---

- TypeScript must pass without `any`-based shortcuts.
- Build and typecheck are mandatory after structural changes.
- Test pure duration calculations and sequence construction as unit tests.
- Test builder invariants: locked discipline, ordering, inheritance, breaks, and time summaries.
- Test timer transitions with a controlled clock.
- Test skipped and unrated exercise averages.
- Test anonymous-user data isolation through RLS policies.
- Add an end-to-end happy path: create plan, start, complete, rate, and open report.
- Do not use `eslint-disable`, `@ts-ignore`, or broad mocks without an explicit justification.
- A visual migration task should include a manual mobile and desktop comparison checklist.
